{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788311694467962587,"compiled_state":{"alias":"wide-wimpy-insect","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"cdb4e94e7f4b0b546be60ac98b78bc4539931c908ce310e2341d773b8d122ee1","event_uuid":"afbcd596-4eee-4e21-a632-111632961ebe","position":{"commit_sha":"48597343545bcd52adf322893029e91ccfe39b0b","position":"1788311470225928052-afbcd596-4eee-4e21-a632-111632961ebe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"21aeb9ee194aa459630419c3f45ae739f1f0aebfe3bde666b4e721edf5a19d0b","event_uuid":"2626b69f-e143-40eb-8e9e-4f5b6d3c8058","position":{"commit_sha":"1941201a68bd7c9a4bddd41b92fd183d5f28d271","position":"1788311694467962586-2626b69f-e143-40eb-8e9e-4f5b6d3c8058"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788311470225928052,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2626b69f-e143-40eb-8e9e-4f5b6d3c8058","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"}],"description":"## Context\n\nTrack I of the stability program (plan: `.scratch/stability-analysis/11-plan-v3.md` §2, evidence `09-complete-picture.md`, grounding `12a/12b/12c`). The defect stream's introduction-side engines, from a 120-bug mechanism-read sample (R2S1, seed 20260831): gate-runtime 20.8%, product-logic representation drift (dominant sub-mechanism of 18.3%), test isolation under ~90-worktree parallelism (15.8%); amplified by 56% of fixes adding a new mechanism. This epic ships the four introduction-reducing programs as six vertical, independently-landable child slices. Track II (loop integrity: gate runtime, store staging) is separate work and NOT in scope here.\n\n## Approach\n\nEach child is a vertical slice: one enforcement mechanism or measurement shipped end-to-end (implementation + tests + docs + `make lint`/CI wiring where applicable). No child consumes an artifact produced by a sibling, so children are order-independent and may run in parallel under `next-batch`. Grounding constraints honored: enforcement is deterministic and harness-neutral (make lint / Verified lane / collection-time checks — never prose or harness hooks); each mechanism added names what bounds it (the ratchet itself is the bound for the epic's own additions); patterns follow the repo's existing generated-registry and shrink-only-baseline precedents.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 (child: MCP parity gate): a deterministic drift gate cross-checks the MCP tool surface against the library facade and fails `make lint` on divergence, with a regression test proving it fires on a seeded mismatch.\n- [ ] AC2 (child: mirror sweep): a committed inventory of remaining hand-maintained representation mirrors exists under reports/, and every live mirror found is either gated/generated or has a linked child/discovered_from ticket.\n- [ ] AC3 (child: subprocess-isolation enforcement): the unit tier fails at collection time when a subprocess-spawning test does not take its isolation root from the harness, with a test proving the check fires.\n- [ ] AC4 (child: cache keying): shared-mutable-state-across-workers defects of the completion-cache class are prevented by per-isolation-root keying/reset, with a regression test for the shared-temp-file pattern.\n- [ ] AC5 (child: mechanism ratchet): `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` runs in `make lint` against a committed shrink-only baseline keyed per (kind, name), failing on any unjustified mechanism addition, with tests covering add/remove/justified-exception paths.\n- [ ] AC6 (child: upstream measurement): the three measurement reads (rework vs change size/files-touched; 20 CI-at-landing regressions; environment failures) are published under reports/ with per-case tables, and the size-rule enforcement decision is recorded either way.\n- [ ] AC7 (documentation): each shipped gate/check is documented where its siblings are (docs/ + the check script's --help), and docs drift gates stay green.\n\nProgram-level exit metrics (scoreboard, not close criteria): per-class bug counts at zero for 30 days per gated mirror / isolation class; additive-fix share ≤30% sustained.\n\n## File impact scope\n\nContainer epic — no direct code; see children's file impacts.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Track I — Reduce defect introduction: drift parity, isolation enforcement, mechanism ratchet, upstream measurement","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["afbcd596-4eee-4e21-a632-111632961ebe","2626b69f-e143-40eb-8e9e-4f5b6d3c8058"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788311694467962587,"uuid":"f20f0d7a-2f43-4889-9b16-9bfc01f0b272"}